# Tersoff potential for monolayer InSe
# Parameter source: Y. Karaaslan, J. Phys. D: Appl. Phys. 58 (2025) 015306.
# One-body (n, beta): Table 1. Two-body (A, B, lambda1, lambda2): Table 2.
# Three-body (lambda3, c, d, h): Table 3. Cutoffs (R, D): Table S1 of the SI.
#
# Usage (units metal):
#   pair_style tersoff
#   pair_coeff * * InSe.tersoff In Se
#
# Mapping notes (validated against the paper's relaxed EIAP geometry, SI Table S8:
# this file reproduces a0 = 4.341 A, d_In-In = 2.537 A, d_In-Se = 2.753 A,
# h = 4.816 A exactly):
# - m = 3, gamma = 1: zeta term = fC(rik) * g(theta) * exp[lambda3^3 (rij - rik)^3].
# - n and beta follow the FIRST (center) element: n(In) = 1.4133,
#   beta(In) = 23.8307e-6; n(Se) = 1.0636, beta(Se) = 5.0263e-6. The Se one-body
#   parameters are shared with GaSe (SI Section S1).
# - Three-body parameters are keyed to the ordered (center i, third atom k) pair,
#   per GULP's pair-wise "boattractive" convention used in the fit: the In-Se-Se
#   set applies to entries In-Se-Se AND In-In-Se; the Se-In-In set to Se-In-In
#   AND Se-Se-In. Entries with (i, k) = In-In or Se-Se are switched off (gamma = 0).
# - Se-Se pairs do not occur within the cutoff and were not parameterized; the
#   Se-Se two-body entry is disabled with A = B = 0.
# - R, D per SI Table S1: In-In 3.45/0.15 A, In-Se 3.45/0.15 A; each row's R, D
#   gate the i-k distance of the zeta sum.
#
# e1 e2 e3  m  gamma  lambda3      c            d        costheta0(h)  n       beta         lambda2  B          R     D     lambda1  A

